{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791122162,"nonce":"FBVGMaFDn30M/UipZuEy80CQijc=","title":"A bordered notch draws its border across the joins between pieces","message":"sd_notch builds its shape as a union: a body plus added pieces (flare\nboxes, the bulge cap max(disk, p.y - base_y), the peak triangle). Each\nadded piece shares an edge with the body exactly. Inside the union near\nthat shared edge, min()/smin() returns the distance to the piece's own\nedge, which is not part of the outline. sdf_notch.wgsl derives its\nborder from inner_sdf = -(d + border), so it rings that internal edge.\n\nSeen as: vertical border lines where the flares meet the body on the\nconcave dropdown; a line across the bulge base on center_bulge_top; a\nline across the triangle base on center_peak_top. Scoop and cut are\nclean because they are subtractions.\n\nFix, proven in ashui's hxsl port (haxe/ashui/core/render/Sdf.hx, sdNotch\nand notchEdge, commit 9cf00a1): extend each added piece a few units into\nthe body, where it is hidden. into = min(8, min(inner_w, inner_h) / 2).\nFlares widen by into toward the body; the bulge cap becomes\nmax(disk, p.y - base_y - into) in the edge's frame; the peak's base\nvertices move down to depth into along its sides, spread =\nhalf_w * (h + into) / h. Any point near a join is then deep inside at\nleast one piece, so the union's interior distance measures to the\noutline.\n\nSecond, smaller defect in the same function: the scoop's hollow unions a\nrect of height max(disk_cy - base_y, 0.001) at full scoop width. When\ndepth \u003c= half_w that rect has zero height, yet smax(d, -hollow, cr)\nstill pulls the top edge down across the whole scoop width. Include the\nrect only when disk_cy - base_y \u003e 0.001.\n\nFound and diagnosed by the ashui session, which rendered notch_demo's\nshapes through BlincApp::render_to_rgba8 with a 2px border.","files":null}]}